WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.359 --> 00:00:04.540
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:09.809
I apologize for the delays during last week,
I always put out notifications about such

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:14.499
events on Twitter and Facebook, make sure
to follow us there so you Fellow Scholars

00:00:14.499 --> 00:00:16.860
know about these well in advance.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:21.520
And I have to say, during this time, I really
missed you and making videos so much!

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:26.960
This video is a quick update on what has happened
since, and I'd also like to assure you that

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:32.099
the next Two Minute Papers episode is already
in the works and is going to arrive soon.

00:00:32.099 --> 00:00:33.690
Very soon.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:38.840
Patreon is a platform where you can support
your favorite creators with monthly recurring

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:41.350
tips and get cool perks in return.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:45.410
We have quite a few supporters who are really
passionate about the show, and during the

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:50.490
making of the last few episodes, we have encountered
severe hardware issues.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:55.899
There were freezes, random restarts, blue
screens of death constantly, and the computer

00:00:55.899 --> 00:01:00.020
was just too unstable to record and edit Two
Minute Papers.

00:01:00.020 --> 00:01:05.080
The technicians checked it out and found that
quite a few parts would have to be replaced,

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:09.700
and I figured that this would be a great time
to replace this old configuration.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:15.299
So, we have ordered the new Two Minute Papers
rig, and the entire purchase happened with

00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:18.440
the help of you, our Patreon supporters!

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:22.720
We were able to replace it effortlessly, which
is just amazing.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:27.780
Words fail me to describe how grateful I am
for your generous support, and I am still

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:28.950
stunned by this.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:34.840
It is just unfathomable to me that I am just
sitting here in a room with a microphone,

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:39.740
having way too much fun with research papers,
and many of you enjoy this series enough to

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:42.590
support it, and it had come to this.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:45.549
You Fellow Scholars make Two Minute Papers
happen.

00:01:45.549 --> 00:01:46.549
Thanks so much.

00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:51.450
I'll try to squeeze in a bit of footage of
the new rig, and transparency above all, will

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:56.520
post the configuration in the video description
box for the more curious minds out there.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:01.560
What I can say at this point, is that this
new rig renders videos three times as quickly

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:02.880
as the previous one.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.729
And even though these are just short videos,
the rendering times for something in full

00:02:07.729 --> 00:02:13.910
HD and 60 fps are surprisingly long even when
run on the graphical card.

00:02:13.910 --> 00:02:15.680
Well, not anymore.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:19.152
So, one more time, thank you so much for supporting
the series.

00:02:19.152 --> 00:02:23.349
This is absolutely amazing, it really is.

00:02:23.349 --> 00:02:28.480
This was a quick update video, the next episode
is coming soon, and I'll try my very best

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:32.379
so we can be back at our regular schedule
of two videos per week.

00:02:32.379 --> 00:02:36.560
Lots of spectacular works are on our list,
stay tuned!

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:41.400
Oh, and by the way, we have Fellow Scholars
watching from all around the world.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:47.420
And in the meantime, some of them have started
translating our episodes to German, Portuguese,

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:49.020
Spanish and Italian.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:53.459
For some reason, I cannot see the names of
the kind people who took their time to contribute,

00:02:53.459 --> 00:02:58.930
so I'd like to kindly thank you for your work,
it makes Two Minute Papers accessible to even

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:01.250
more people, which is amazing.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:04.850
Thanks for watching, and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

